<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.alphalete.icd-onboarding-no-shows</string>

    <!-- Install on the box holding this office's ApplicantStream session:
             lucy rerun install_icd_onboarding_no_shows_agent (machine "Lucy 3")
         NOTE ON COMMENTS IN THIS FILE: never write two hyphens together inside
         an XML comment. It ends the comment early and makes the plist
         unparseable to plistlib even though plutil still accepts it, which
         shows up as a Hub card that cries wolf forever. The blueink docs plist
         carried exactly that defect from the day it was written until
         2026-11-16, so no command line flags are spelled out here. -->

    <!-- Path is the laptop placeholder; install_agent.py rewrites it to that
         machine's repo path. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/deploy/icd_onboarding_no_shows.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PYTHONPATH</key>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- 9:15pm EVERY DAY, machine LOCAL time. No Weekday key: a training day
         can fall on any day of the week, and the board is seeded from whoever
         is scheduled to start, not from a Monday.

         THE EVENING is the point. The training day has to have happened and a
         recruiter has to have marked the Show Up radio, so this runs after the
         office closes. It lands before the next morning's sends: Blue Ink goes
         out at 7:30am, and this is the column that stops it mailing documents
         to somebody who did not come (Megan, 2026-11-16: "run it daily").

         ONCE A DAY, not hourly, because it is the seven page calendar walk the
         hourly board run deliberately stopped doing. TIME KNOB: edit
         StartCalendarInterval here, not the wrapper.

         21:15, NOT ON THE HALF HOUR. com.alphalete.icd-onboarding fires at
         :30 of every hour from 6:30 to 20:30 and drives the same
         ApplicantStream profile, so the wrapper's own overlap guard skips
         this walk whenever the two meet. Set to 19:30 it met the board run
         every single night: it fired on time on 2026-11-19 at 19:30:05,
         skipped, and would have gone on skipping forever while looking
         installed. 21:15 is 45 minutes past the last board run of the day,
         still the same evening, and still ahead of Blue Ink at 7:30am.
         Any new time here goes BETWEEN the :30 fires, never on one. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>21</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>15</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/output/logs/icd-onboarding-no-shows.launchd.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/output/logs/icd-onboarding-no-shows.launchd.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
